1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,125
Is This Seat Taken?

3
00:00:03,125 --> 00:00:05,771
The school library is busy after lunch.

4
00:00:05,771 --> 00:00:10,156
I carry two heavy books between the tables until I spot Emma beside an empty chair.

5
00:00:10,156 --> 00:00:11,781
Is this seat taken?

6
00:00:12,002 --> 00:00:12,921
It's yours.

7
00:00:12,921 --> 00:00:14,619
Just watch out for my backpack.

8
00:00:14,619 --> 00:00:16,358
It's trying to take over the floor.

9
00:00:16,636 --> 00:00:19,119
I sit down and put my books on the table.

10
00:00:19,119 --> 00:00:21,171
One is about mountain climbing.

11
00:00:21,171 --> 00:00:24,359
The other is about a detective who loses his own keys.

12
00:00:24,359 --> 00:00:26,286
I'm looking for something funny.

13
00:00:26,498 --> 00:00:28,188
Then I'd start with the detective.

14
00:00:28,188 --> 00:00:31,135
Losing your keys while solving a mystery sounds pretty good.

15
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:33,299
I open the first page.

16
00:00:33,299 --> 00:00:35,935
The detective is locked outside his office.

17
00:00:35,935 --> 00:00:38,830
Emma leans over, and we both start laughing.

18
00:00:38,830 --> 00:00:42,497
We quickly cover our mouths because everyone else is reading quietly.

19
00:00:42,772 --> 00:00:44,755
Sounds like you found a good one.

20
00:00:44,755 --> 00:00:46,484
Would you like to check it out?

21
00:00:46,756 --> 00:00:48,437
Yes, please.

22
00:00:48,437 --> 00:00:49,833
When is it due?

23
00:00:50,116 --> 00:00:51,620
In two weeks.

24
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:53,495
The date is on this slip.

25
00:00:53,495 --> 00:00:56,422
You can renew it if nobody else is waiting for it.

26
00:00:56,642 --> 00:00:58,029
Can I borrow it after you?

27
00:00:58,029 --> 00:00:59,300
No spoilers, though.

28
00:00:59,572 --> 00:01:00,680
Deal.

29
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:04,701
I put the library slip inside the book and check my pockets before we leave.

30
00:01:04,922 --> 00:01:06,164
What are you looking for?

31
00:01:06,436 --> 00:01:07,909
My house key.

32
00:01:07,909 --> 00:01:10,273
I don't want to end up like this detective.

33
00:01:10,564 --> 00:01:12,576
A very sensible decision.

34
00:01:12,796 --> 00:01:15,258
My key is exactly where it belongs.

35
00:01:15,258 --> 00:01:17,331
The detective would be impressed.

36
00:01:17,331 --> 00:01:19,571
Now he just needs to find his.
